Plate is square, about 26 cm across (it spans roughly 455 px, so about 17 px per cm). The potato cubes cover an area of roughly 270x170 px, or about 16x10 cm, but they are sparse. I count about 30 cubes, each around 1.5-2 cm (roughly 2.5-4 cm³ per cube). Taking about 3.5 cm³ per cube gives roughly 105 cm³. At about 0.65 g/cm³ for fried potato, allowing for irregular shapes, that is about 70 g.

There is a little visible oil sheen, which is negligible, so I'm folding it into the potatoes.

